1
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:12,900
Look, know it and step back, okay?

2
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:28,620
Like someone is calling out to you,
a rainy afternoon after the rain stops,

3
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:35,280
walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:42,420
That mysterious feeling I had back then

5
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the arcade guide tiles,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,500
I tried walking only on the black parts.

7
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,100
Even the politicians with their self-important faces,
and the blue-haired aunties who look down on everyone,

10
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning that corner over there.

11
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kameari
surely Kameari is there!

13
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,060
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

15
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,220
Start your life over.

16
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,080
Don't let Honda get away!

17
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,400
Bleh, bleh.

18
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:51,720
Leave it to me.

19
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,400
Let's do it.

20
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,780
Aaaaaaah.

21
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:58,820
Aaaaaaah.

22
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:04,980
Eeeeeeeh.

23
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:18,500
Aaah! Don't you dare
take the police lightly!

24
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:18,660
Excuse me!

25
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,600
You idiot!

26
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,340
What on earth are you all thinking?!

27
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:28,080
Ohara, you're not planning to abandon
your supervision of him, are you?

28
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,280
Honestly, I don't even know what to say.

29
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,500
Excuse me.

30
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:41,300
That lecture today went on a bit long

31
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:42,600
Hey, Buchi,

32
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,460
If it weren't for you,

33
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:50,440
my life would have turned
out so much differently.

34
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,760
Yeah, it must have been hard.

35
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,520
I nearly got fired from my second-term post,
you know.

36
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:02,480
Well, there's no point dwelling
on what's already happened.

37
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:04,940
You've got to live life
with a positive attitude.

38
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:09,340
How carefree can you possibly be?

39
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,180
Now, now.

40
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:18,080
Senpai, Nakagawa here.
The prototype you asked for is finally done.

41
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:28,640
Here it is! This is the ultimate PC game. What
on earth is this? Nakagawa's company developed it.

42
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:35,040
It's a groundbreaking PC game. It's nothing
like the games where you raise girls or pets.

43
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:37,640
No, this is a game where you raise yourself.

44
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,120
Raise yourself?

45
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,160
What do you mean?

46
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,860
In other words,
you input all of your personal data

47
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:45,740
and turn it into a game character.

48
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:51,160
Then you can simulate that
person's future on the computer.

49
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:53,780
There are too many loanwords.
I don't really get it.

50
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:57,040
So it's basically the Game
of Life on a computer, then.

51
00:03:57,040 --> 00:04:00,940
And it shows you a future that's
pretty close to reality, right?

52
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:06,540
The Chief won't get it just by hearing about it.
Let's try it out.

53
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:07,940
Let's do that.

54
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:15,000
This game already has all of the
senior's data entered as a sample.

55
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:20,260
When you start the game,
the main character appears.

56
00:04:21,020 --> 00:04:22,620
He looks just like Ryotsu!

57
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:25,300
That's right, because this is me.

58
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,340
What?

59
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:30,060
For example, let's say you drop
some money in front of a senior.

60
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:31,100
And then,

61
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:33,560
Jackpot! There's 5,000 yen on the ground!

62
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,080
Lucky!

63
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,000
Hey! A police officer of all people,

64
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,820
do you think it's okay
to pocket lost property?!

65
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,580
Stop it! Please calm down!

66
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,900
This is a game! Just a game!

67
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,840
Right, I got carried away.

68
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:48,700
Yes! I did it.

69
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:50,920
Hey, what are these numbers?

70
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:55,240
They show your current happiness,
assets, and status as numbers.

71
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,780
I found 5,000 yen, so your assets are 5,000.

72
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,800
Your happiness has gone up to 10.

73
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:02,600
So my status hasn't changed.

74
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,040
There's more to it.

75
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:06,140
The Chief just came out.

76
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:09,260
Ryotsu, what were you doing here?

77
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:11,980
Chief it's nothing.

78
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,580
I've got nothing to hide.

79
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:15,120
Nice weather today, isn't it?

80
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:20,140
His excuses are just like Ryo-chan's.

81
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:22,200
We have the same personality, after all.

82
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,740
I saw that, Ryotsu!

83
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,860
A police officer of all people,

84
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:28,400
do you think you can just
seize evidence like that?

85
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:30,320
Chief, please calm down.

86
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,500
Even the lines are the same.

87
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:33,260
You there!

88
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,660
I'll hold on to this.

89
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:39,820
Damn it.

90
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:42,340
My happiness and assets are back to zero.

91
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:43,860
Well, of course.

92
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:46,980
From now on, I'll marry a rich girl

93
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,920
and boost every single number!

94
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:51,500
No way.

95
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:52,520
Mine's in there too.

96
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,600
Speaking of rich people,

97
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,620
Reiko.

98
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:01,320
Hey, what are you doing?

99
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,580
As long as he's rich, that's fine, right?

100
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:11,640
All three numbers are shooting up fast.

101
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:13,180
That's more like it.

102
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:16,720
In just one month!

103
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:16,980
No way...

104
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:22,340
The company started with your
wife's dowry went bankrupt.

105
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:29,220
Damn, this is nothing!

106
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:31,920
Then I'll make a comeback
as a police officer!

107
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:34,100
Heh, it's no big deal!

108
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:42,040
Whoa! I've been laid off from the police!

109
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:46,943
Ha this is great! Even if it's just a game,

110
00:06:46,993 --> 00:06:48,720
this is so satisfying!

111
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,540
Hahahahaha!

112
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:51,940
Look!

113
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:55,040
He's gone desperate and
started robbing a bank!

114
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:55,900
Hand over the money!

115
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,920
Hey, what do you think you're doing?!

116
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:01,800
I can't help it!
The character is moving on its own!

117
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,640
He went and stole 330 million!

118
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:08,620
You utter fool!

119
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:12,340
Ugh, I'm never working
another day in my life!

120
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:14,800
What a guy!

121
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:17,040
Looks like he's really
developed a taste for it!

122
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:20,520
Ryotsu, turn yourself in quietly!

123
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:21,940
No way!

124
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:23,920
Hey, get back here, Ryotsu!

125
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:32,520
Your persuasion still needs work.
Stop mixing up the game with reality!
Look, this time he's got a gun!

126
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,800
He's planning to hit a cash transport truck.

127
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,020
He'll vanish into the shadows.

128
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,100
He got shot.

129
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:49,120
They say in 2005 the laws changed
and defense was strengthened.

130
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,500
Don't go making predictions on your own.

131
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:55,260
Game over

132
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:58,720
This is pretty interesting, isn't it?

133
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,880
This is well made, Nakagawa.

134
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:01,360
Attention!

135
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,160
How could this happen?

136
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:07,280
At this rate,
I'm the only one who's miserable!

137
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,780
All of you, join in too.

138
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:12,200
It's fine, the data is perfect.

139
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:14,040
Am I going to play too?

140
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:14,840
Me too.

141
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,100
Do I have to play too?

142
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:19,760
That's right,
and everyone starts at age three.

143
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:22,420
But shouldn't we have been
born in different eras?

144
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:25,080
It's properly linked, so it's fine.

145
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,280
Aww, how cute.

146
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,500
Hey, Ryo-san,

147
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:33,220
since we're doing this, could we start
with different conditions than now?

148
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:37,240
If not,
it's no fun to look at my future, right?

149
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,120
Yeah, you've got a point.

150
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:42,600
Alright,
Ryotsu starts out as a rich young master.

151
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:47,200
But Nakagawa and Reiko
start out as poor folks, so.

152
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,960
Why's that?

153
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:53,420
You two get to experience the hardship
of crawling up from the bottom.

154
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:56,580
Alright, starting with Ryotsu.

155
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,460
I don't know where my house is.

156
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:03,260
Getting lost in your own family's yard?

157
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:05,160
Well, I'm not used to it.

158
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,560
Daddy, Daddy.

159
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:09,040
He's gone out of the house!

160
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:11,640
That's a bit much, isn't it?

161
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:15,020
W-w-what's going to happen to me?

162
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:19,380
Looks like a kind person took me in.

163
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:22,420
And as he grows up,

164
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:24,500
he becomes a police officer,

165
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:28,860
or lives an ordinary but happy family life.

166
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,900
What? That's no different
from how things are now!

167
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,780
Well, I guess that's just how it goes.

168
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:37,800
And we went to the trouble of
having him born into a rich family!

169
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:39,740
Alright, next up is Reiko.

170
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:42,320
Three-year-old Reiko?

171
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:46,500
Her clothes are shabby, but she's cute.

172
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:51,700
No matter how cute she is, she's this poor?

173
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:54,180
Wonderful.

174
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:57,160
This is the ideal girl
I've been searching for.

175
00:09:57,160 --> 00:10:00,520
Hey, kid, how'd you like to be in our movie?

176
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:02,780
Mom.

177
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:08,280
Since she's a beautiful girl, a film director spots her,
and she debuts as a child actress?

178
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:12,400
That movie became a
record-breaking smash hit.

179
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:14,940
Reiko instantly became a national star.

180
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:15,720
Hold on, hold on.

181
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,220
Not only that, she expanded into Hollywood.

182
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:19,860
becoming a world-class superstar.

183
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:24,860
She gets taken in by the President and
becomes a secretary at the White House.

184
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:27,480
Then she's even more amazing than she is now,
isn't she?

185
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,100
Charisma and talent are what set her apart.

186
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:30,980
No way.

187
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:32,380
Damn it!

188
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:35,300
Alright, then Nakagawa's going to be even, even
Translation>
(continued)

189
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:37,940
made into hyper ultra special poverty.

190
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,540
It starts with him
living in a drainage pipe.

191
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,100
Isn't that a bit too harsh?

192
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:45,860
His reality is already too privileged,
so this is fine.

193
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,460
The rich-kid role, all set.

194
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:51,140
Amuko is...

195
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:56,020
Hold on! No way!
I'll make sure nobody can get through!

196
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:59,140
At this rate, nobody can get close.

197
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:00,520
That's awful.

198
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:03,460
Construction's started.

199
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:05,000
Hey, you.

200
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,020
Yes, president.

201
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:06,900
Who's that kid?

202
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:11,300
Hey! I won't stand for
such a convenient setup!

203
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:15,220
Alright,
let's start from where he's drifting at sea.

204
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,740
Hey, what about that girl?

205
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:22,760
Why does it always conveniently
find only rich people?

206
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:24,300
Now, now.

207
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:28,800
No matter what the settings are,
Nakagawa seems destined to become rich.

208
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,860
He must have been born
under a very lucky star.

209
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:33,900
It's even frightening to me.

210
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,420
Not interesting.

211
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:37,540
Then next, it's the Chief's turn.

212
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:39,440
You idiot!

213
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:42,720
What on earth are you doing, Tonda?

214
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:45,240
Sorry, Chief Ohara.

215
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,840
Chief Ohara.

216
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:49,580
What's going on?

217
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:53,353
I see, the game's still running with the
setting where the senior officer died earlier,

218
00:11:53,403 --> 00:11:55,300
so it's still going.

219
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:55,880
What?

220
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:58,722
So what you're saying is,
if this guy hadn't existed,

221
00:11:58,772 --> 00:12:01,580
I'd be chief by now?

222
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:03,200
Looks that way.

223
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:06,660
I want to see more.
Show me what happens next.

224
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:08,200
Sure, I guess.

225
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,960
Amazing! He's even risen to
Police Commissioner General!

226
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:13,220
What?

227
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:13,420
What?

228
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:14,980
How about it, Ryotsu?

229
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:18,560
This is what my true ability looks like,
if only you weren't around.

230
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:19,980
Hahahaha!

231
00:12:19,980 --> 00:12:23,980
Now, who was it that said not
to mix up games and reality?

232
00:12:24,060 --> 00:12:24,920
Idiot!

233
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:28,340
It's proof that my life
changed because of you.

234
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,940
With this plague god of a man...

235
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:33,480
No way! Don't go deciding I'm a plague god!

236
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:38,160
Then without that senior officer,
what would have become of me?

237
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:41,520
Right, go on, show him, Ryotsu.

238
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:46,520
You've been promoted to Chief of
the Traffic Mobile Unit headquarters.

239
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:47,480
Really?

240
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:51,680
Just because he ran into Ryotsu, it's
the difference between heaven and earth.

241
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:55,180
That's cruel, senpai.
I knew it, he's a plague god after all!

242
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,780
What did I ever do to deserve this?

243
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:01,760
Then let's see how the others turned out.

244
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:04,040
How about Sakonji-san, for example?

245
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:08,620
After winning a gold medal at the Olympics,

246
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,240
greatly successful as a K-1 fighter.

247
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:14,480
Mote-matsu's life.

248
00:13:15,540 --> 00:13:16,720
You devil!

249
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,000
What are you doing, Chief?

250
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,700
Don't "what are you doing" me!

251
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:24,260
Everyone's unhappy just
because they met you!

252
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:27,200
It's just a game simulation,
for crying out loud.

253
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,480
Still, it's pretty close to reality!

254
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:31,180
Take responsibility! Take responsibility!

255
00:13:31,180 --> 00:13:32,380
That's absurd!

256
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:37,820
Then, conversely, let's try it with
you meeting Senpai much earlier.

257
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:38,820
Yeah, that's right.

258
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:42,360
It may not be only Senpai's
responsibility, though.

259
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:44,500
Then how about Komachi-chan?

260
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:45,500
Let's do it.

261
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:50,720
At age three, he met a senior
who was the neighborhood bully,

262
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:53,582
and since he had no one else,

263
00:13:53,632 --> 00:13:55,140
he reluctantly married that senior.

264
00:13:55,140 --> 00:13:59,260
He paved over his family's rice paddy to build a building,
but failed to run it.

265
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:02,080
He's buried in debt and doesn't
even have a place to live.

266
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:04,060
No way!

267
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:07,240
See? Ryotsu, it's all your fault.

268
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,240
That's not true!

269
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:12,500
Some people might have become
unhappy even without meeting me, right?

270
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:15,340
Then let's check on some other people.

271
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:17,400
Then how about Ozaki Models?

272
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:19,780
He's the president of
a large model-kit chain.

273
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,560
Then how about Ryo's aunt?

274
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:24,540
She won the All-Japan Ideal Wife Contest.

275
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:26,840
No way, what about my dad?

276
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:30,760
Ryōze works at a large corporation and is the
head of the Asahi Shopping District Association.

277
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:32,800
Then what about that dog?

278
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:35,920
A wealthy man took him in,
and he lives in luxury.

279
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:37,720
That's ridiculous!

280
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:41,240
Then, Terai. What would happen
to Terai if he never met me?

281
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:42,780
Terai-san?

282
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:46,800
Look. Terai hasn't
changed from before, has he?

283
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:48,900
But look. His happiness level.

284
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:52,060
It went from 60% to 62%.

285
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:55,000
It went up 2.2%.

286
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:59,560
So it's all my fault?

287
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,500
That's not true at all.

288
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:04,040
Maria.

289
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,464
Please. If I were a real woman,

290
00:15:06,514 --> 00:15:09,380
please run it to see how things
would turn out between me and Ryo-sama.

291
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,220
Well then, here we go.

292
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:14,960
I'm counting on you.

293
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:18,940
They got married and
everything turned out happily.

294
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:22,400
They're so lovey-dovey.

295
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:26,020
Really. Their happiness keeps climbing.

296
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,230
Thanks to Maria,

297
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,580
he arrested a suspect on the
top international wanted list.

298
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:34,240
he even won a 300 million yen lottery.

299
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:37,700
and was promoted all the way to
Criminal Investigation Division Chief.

300
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:39,640
Everything has been going wonderfully.

301
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:44,060
Plus, thanks to Maria being so dependable,

302
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:46,760
he wouldn't cause any trouble
for those around him at all.

303
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:48,620
There's nothing better than this.

304
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:51,120
Maria's so happy.

305
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,000
How about it, Ryotsu?

306
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:56,560
Why don't you just go ahead
and actually marry Maria?

307
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,700
That'd be great.

308
00:15:57,700 --> 00:16:00,300
Yeah, Ryo-chan, that'd be great!

309
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:03,940
Ryo-sama, let's get married right away!

310
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:05,640
Yeah.

311
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:10,280
There's no way that could happen!
Because you're...

312
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,980
But you're a man!

313
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:19,220
Yeah, if you weren't a man,
it would be a problem.

314
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:23,320
That's right, Ryo-san.
It's for everyone. Congratulations.

315
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:24,700
Senpai, congratulations.

316
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:25,780
Maria Anjaro, congratulations.

317
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:28,160
Please take good care of Senpai.

318
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:29,500
Good for you, Ryo-san.

319
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:35,500
No way!
I absolutely refuse to marry a man! Help me!

320
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:40,860
Wait! Ryo-san!
Let's build a happy home together!

321
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:47,480
I said no means no! This topic is over!
Move on to the next one! The next topic!

322
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,860
The man with the seven-colored voice

323
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:01,980
Good morning.

324
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:23,300
Looks like Tokyo-kun is listening.

325
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:26,080
I was surprised too when
I woke up this morning.

326
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,200
Are you all right? Senpai.

327
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,300
This is nothing.

328
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:39,440
Even Ryo-san seems to
have taken a lot of damage

329
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,860
So you were just an ordinary human.

330
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:44,100
Of course, obviously.

331
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:47,400
Ryo-san, that voice...

332
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:49,660
W-what's wrong?

333
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:52,400
It's just like Chief Ohara's.

334
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,100
Creepy.

335
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:56,140
Like the Chief's voice?
Do I really sound that similar?

336
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:59,360
Anyone would say that voice is the Chief's.

337
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:03,020
Testing, testing, one, two.

338
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,360
Good morning, everyone.

339
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,400
Just kidding!

340
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:07,100
It's true.

341
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:11,460
Yes, Kōen-mae Police Box.

342
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,220
It's the station chief.

343
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:16,100
Chief Ohara hasn't arrived yet, though.

344
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,280
I've caught a cold.

345
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:23,100
Hello? It's me, Ohara. That voice is the station chief's, isn't it?
What do you want from me?

346
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:28,100
Is that any way to behave, Ohara?

347
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:31,480
If you have a complaint,
come here, you idiot station chief!

348
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:36,440
I won't forget this.
I'm the grudge-holding type, you know.

349
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,960
Sure. I'm Ohara.

350
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:44,960
How awful.

351
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,380
Who cares!

352
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:50,040
Alright, make calls everywhere
using the Chief's voice!

353
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:52,080
S-senpai...

354
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,220
I don't know anything about it.

355
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,120
Hello, Sakai Sushi.

356
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,740
It's Chief Ohara!

357
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:04,420
Yes, it's Ohara. Ten premium sushi platters,
and put it all on the department's tab!

358
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:08,700
Yes, Ozaki Models.

359
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:10,800
It's Chief Ohara!

360
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:18,700
Sorry, but please deliver a radio-controlled helicopter,
a Battleship Yamato model kit, and the Combat figure set to Ryotsu's place.

361
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:21,500
Of course, I'll pay for all of it.

362
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,600
You're wondering why?

363
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:28,500
It's a reward for Officer
Ryotsu's hard work every day.

364
00:19:28,980 --> 00:19:33,180
You've gone too far, Ryo-chan.

365
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:34,960
That's right, senpai.

366
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:37,200
Shut up! This is payback for
all the times you've annoyed me!

367
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:40,440
Alright, next I'll call the
Police Commissioner General!

368
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:46,460
See, Ryo-san?
It's because you do bad things.

369
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,000
Shut up!

370
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:50,380
His voice changed again!

371
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:52,100
This time it's the Chief's voice.

372
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,820
What did you say?

373
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:56,540
It's true.

374
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:59,080
That's strange. What's going on?

375
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:03,160
If I press my throat like this,
because it hurts...

376
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:07,080
It hurts...

377
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:08,660
Well, of course.

378
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:10,960
If you strangle yourself, you'll die.

379
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:13,040
You don't even understand that much.

380
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,720
It changed again.

381
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:16,240
The voice got higher.

382
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:20,420
I see, I think I've
figured out how it works.

383
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:26,900
See, now your voice has
gone higher again, right?

384
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:28,140
It really has.

385
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:31,180
Apparently it changes when you
touch this spot on the throat.

386
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:32,840
When you press one finger lower,

387
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:36,100
it drops an octave, and when you go higher,

388
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,140
it gets higher.

389
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:40,180
And you can adjust the voice with
the balance between left and right.

390
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:41,460
That's amazing.

391
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:43,720
A man with a voice of seven colors

392
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:46,080
Alright, if I do it like this,
and like this,

393
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:49,940
I bought a brand-new Ferrari, you know.

394
00:20:49,940 --> 00:20:52,580
I got tired of it,
so I'll give it to you, senpai.

395
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,700
How about this voice?

396
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:56,280
Sounds just like Kē-chan.

397
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:57,840
Amazing that it actually works.

398
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:00,020
And if you do it like this...

399
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:05,160
It's Ryo-chan, the manliest idol
cop and the most popular one, right?

400
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:07,880
It's Reiko-san.

401
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:09,020
Somehow I don't like this.

402
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:10,340
Next...

403
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:14,220
I live my life by my own principles,
you know.

404
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:15,580
It's Terai!

405
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:19,180
Do I really sound like Hayashi or Kobehei?

406
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:20,740
And also,

407
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:24,360
Oi oi, it's a Honda from the bōsōzoku!
Zooming full throttle!

408
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:28,200
Uuugh, Saorii... Sakon Chitatsunosuke-de!

409
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:32,040
Ryo-sama, it's me, Maria!

410
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:33,420
Just kidding.

411
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:36,180
Good morning.

412
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:37,600
Chief.

413
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:39,000
Good morning, sir.

414
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:42,240
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

415
00:21:43,780 --> 00:21:45,700
What a strange fellow you are.

416
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:46,220
Thanks for your order!

417
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:48,920
Chief Ohara?

418
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:51,500
Ten servings of premium sushi, here you go.

419
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,160
What?

420
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:54,960
I don't remember ordering
anything like that.

421
00:21:55,860 --> 00:21:58,760
But it was definitely your voice, Chief.

422
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:01,380
Even if you say that,
I have no memory of it, so I didn't.

423
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:02,060
No way.

424
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:02,920
Then...

425
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:06,160
Chief!

426
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:08,580
Your order, the gift for Ryo-san.

427
00:22:08,580 --> 00:22:09,500
Here you are.

428
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:10,300
What?

429
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,860
The Chief has a good side after all,
doesn't he?

430
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:14,720
No way.

431
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:17,300
I would never do something like that.

432
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:18,860
Stop being so bashful.

433
00:22:18,860 --> 00:22:21,080
No, it wasn't me!

434
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:22,880
But on the phone, you...

435
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:24,060
Ohara-kun.

436
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:27,140
You've arrived at just the right time.

437
00:22:27,140 --> 00:22:29,720
Something strange has happened.

438
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:31,760
Ohara-kun.

439
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:36,240
A transfer order has come through for a posting at the end of the sea,
you see.

440
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:38,700
We've decided you'll go
there by helicopter right away.

441
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:39,300
What?

442
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:44,580
C-Chief, why would I be sent to
some place at the end of the sea?

443
00:22:44,580 --> 00:22:47,080
After saying all that on the phone.

444
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:49,580
On the phone?
I don't know what you're talking about.

445
00:22:50,420 --> 00:22:51,220
Ryo-chan.

446
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:53,820
Ryotsu, do you know something?

447
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:57,160
Ryotsu, was this your doing?

448
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:59,080
No, I didn't do anything at all.

449
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:03,440
What, your voice has turned into a woman's!

450
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:06,520
Senpai has become a man with seven voices.

451
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:08,780
What? What do you mean by that?

452
00:23:10,880 --> 00:23:13,180
Ryo-san, running away won't help!

453
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,140
So, this is how it works.

454
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:17,520
If you do this here...

455
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:20,320
W-wait, stop it, Nakagawa, stop!

456
00:23:20,620 --> 00:23:22,240
M-my voice!

457
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:24,860
Then, if you do this here...

458
00:23:24,860 --> 00:23:27,220
I said stop, look, Nakagawa!

459
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:28,900
And if you do it like this...

460
00:23:28,900 --> 00:23:29,740
Hold still, you!

461
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:31,260
I won't let you off easy!

462
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:34,860
You idiot!
You've gone and left that head totally bare!

463
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:39,200
That's how Ryo-chan was able to
freely switch between his seven voices.

464
00:23:41,100 --> 00:23:43,860
Make sure you pay for ten
servings of premium sushi.

465
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:46,360
And I'm taking your model kits too.

466
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:49,220
Ryotsu, I hope you're prepared for this.

467
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:51,960
You're the one who's
going to the depths of hell.

468
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:54,860
You, you're the kind of man who...

469
00:23:54,860 --> 00:23:56,280
Please stop, Chief.

470
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:58,960
Shut up, you idiot!

471
00:23:58,960 --> 00:23:59,580
This guy.

472
00:23:59,580 --> 00:24:01,340
I'm getting dizzy.

473
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:03,360
I won't forgive you this time.

474
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:03,820
Quiet!

475
00:24:03,820 --> 00:24:05,300
You fool.

476
00:24:05,300 --> 00:24:07,080
You'll remember this, mark my words.

477
00:24:09,220 --> 00:24:13,900
I don't even know what's going
on in my own brain anymore.

478
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:15,160
Somebody help me.

479
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:21,640
I kicked the alarm clock and
stubbed my pinky toe, ow ow

480
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:30,040
Drew my eyebrows on somehow,
then dash, dash, dash to the station!

481
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:35,520
Packed train, a nap on some old man's back.

482
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:41,840
Another hard week, and as they say,
"you reap what you sow," fair enough.

483
00:24:43,180 --> 00:24:46,680
But I'm acting all composed
with one hand in my pocket,

484
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:49,420
a beef bowl, extra sauce, extra soggy.

485
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:52,780
All the irritation from endless overtime,

486
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:56,360
gets cleared right up with more irritation!

487
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:02,220
Every day is no problem!

488
00:25:03,020 --> 00:25:06,080
I love a girl like me!

489
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:12,940
Every day is no problem-brave,
hearts flying on Monday.

490
00:25:13,360 --> 00:25:17,400
Mandeck, mandeck, no problem-brave!

491
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:24,260
Whoa! Why does misfortune keep
piling onto me one after another?

492
00:25:24,580 --> 00:25:29,360
What? According to the fortune-teller,
today is the worst day of my life?

493
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:33,420
I see, so as long as today ends,
this misfortune will end too, right?

494
00:25:33,420 --> 00:25:36,040
Next time: The Worst Day of My Life.

495
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:40,860
Thank you for watching.

